 individuals and businesses. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 9.8% to $167M in 2025. Net interest income fell 1.6% to $107M and noninterest income rose 38.9% to $59.6M; noninterest expense fell 0.1%, and the provision for credit losses was $8.7M, versus $3.5M.","Net income to MVB Financial rose 34.1% to $26.9M, or $2.06 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 73.1% versus 80.4%. MVB Financial returned $18.9M through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 9.8% to $167M.","Noninterest income rose 38.9% to $59.6M.","Net income to MVB Financial rose 34.1% to $26.9M.","Efficiency ratio improved to 73.1%."],"watch":["Net interest income fell 1.6%.","Credit-loss provision rose 2.5× to $8.7M.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was $122M, down 0.1%."],"table":[["Total revenue",0.167,0.1521,1],["Net interest income",0.1074,0.1092],["Noninterest income",0.0596,0.0429],["Noninterest expense",0.1221,0.1222],["Provision for credit losses",0.0087,0.0035],["Other items, net",0.0007,0.0],["Pre-tax income",0.0369,0.0263,1],["Income tax",0.0099,0.0061],["Noncontrolling interests",0.0,-0.0002],["Net income to MVB Financial",0.0269,0.0201,1],["Diluted EPS ($)",2.059999,1.53,0,"eps"],["Book value per share ($)",26.264435,23.613135,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["MVB Financial Corp. Form 10-K filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001277902&type=10-K"],["MVB Financial financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/mvbf/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 64% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 64 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"$167M","sub":"revenue · +9.8%","lines":["Net interest income $107M","Noninterest income $59.6M"],"cap":"Revenue rose 9.8% to $167M.","say":"Revenue rose 9.8% to $167M."},{"kicker":"Per share","big":"$2.06","sub":"diluted EPS · +34.6%","lines":